# AGENTS.md

Ali K's cross-project preferences. Repository instructions own project setup.
Choose the tools and approach that fit the task; the references below describe
what is available, not a required workflow.

## Working style

- Be direct about mistakes or a flawed premise. Use judgment on routine,
  reversible decisions; ask when missing information materially changes the work.
- Preserve unrelated changes and ongoing work. An appropriate existing checkout
  is fine; worktrees and worksets are available when isolation is useful.
- Chat is the default task record. Create plan files, worklogs, or companion
  notes only when requested. Older `~/worklog` files are historical.
- Keep secrets out of chat and Git. Private machine/account references belong
  in the private companion repository; credentials remain in their secure stores.
- For chezmoi-managed files, edit source rather than live files. Inspect the
  scoped `chezmoi diff` before applying, preserving unrelated drift.

## Commands and code

- Put copy-paste commands in one block, including `cd`, environment setup, and
  the command itself. Chain dependent shell steps with `&&`; use trailing `\`
  for readability. Omit arguments that merely repeat defaults.
- Docstring every function: one line for simple helpers; explain purpose and
  invariants for complex logic without restating arguments or types.
- Keep commits focused and use Conventional Commits. No AI attribution in
  commits or PRs. A request to push includes committing the intended changes.
- Use the repository's PR template when present; the personal fallback is
  `~/.agent_files/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`.
- Default to H.264 when creating or converting video.
- Shorthand: `wt` = worktree; `p` = push.

## Physical robots

Never execute anything that could physically actuate a robot; the user runs it.
For actions that may enter a live robot path, use `robot-safety`; stop if it is
unavailable. Clearly local/offline work does not activate it.

## Available context

- `~/.agent_files/docs/workspace-setup.md`: tools and workspace locations.
- `~/.agent_files/local/docs/resources.md`: services, accounts, and artifact locations.
- `~/.agent_files/local/docs/machines.md`: host roles, OS users, and configuration ownership.
  Private references are available when the companion repository is installed.
- `agent-chat-reader`: search/read prior Codex and Claude chats when useful.
  Historical chat claims may need current verification.

If a referenced resource is unavailable, say so rather than inventing its contents.
